    "introduction": "Babcock International provides engineering, support and specialist systems for defence and other critical operations. Its activities span marine, nuclear, land and aviation, including maintaining equipment, supporting naval infrastructure and integrating complex systems. Customers include governments and organisations that need assets to remain available and safe over long operating lives. Revenue comes through contracts covering projects and ongoing services, often requiring specialised staff and facilities. Its model depends on technical capability, security requirements and close understanding of customer operations. Contract execution, labour availability and programme timing influence profitability, while defence priorities and infrastructure commitments shape the pipeline of future work.",
